    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0264" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg132"/>

                <head>No. 105 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d105-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Independence, Missouri</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-27">June 27th,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Ed</hi>: …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I wanted you to come with me to the meeting with Marshal Stalin and Prime Minister Churchill which will take place next month. But, since I shall
                    be away during the Congressional hearings [on the Charter of the United
                    Nations], I have reluctantly agreed to your suggestion that you remain in
                    Washington while I am away. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Truman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d105-f1" n="1" xml:id="d105-f1-content">
                <p>For the full text of this letter, in which Truman accepted Stettinius’ resignation as Secretary of State, see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >xiii</hi>, p. 15, from which source this extract is printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
